---
/**
 * Starlight `ThemeProvider` override — pins the site to the light theme.
 *
 * Starlight's default reads localStorage / prefers-color-scheme and flips to a
 * very dark palette (#0F051D), which is what made the content pages feel so much
 * heavier than the homepage. The site now has one look, matching the landing
 * page, so there is no dark variant to switch to.
 *
 * `window.StarlightThemeProvider.updatePickers` is still defined as a no-op:
 * Starlight's ThemeSelect calls it inline, and while we override that component
 * away too, keeping the shim means nothing throws if it ever returns.
 */
---

{/* Inlined to avoid a flash of the wrong theme. */}
<script is:inline>
  document.documentElement.dataset.theme = 'light';
  // Clear any preference stored before the site became light-only, otherwise
  // returning visitors would keep re-applying a theme that no longer exists.
  try {
    localStorage.removeItem('starlight-theme');
  } catch {}
  window.StarlightThemeProvider = { updatePickers() {} };
</script>
